(version 1)

; atlas-duck sandbox worker profile (spec 9.4, macOS).
;
; The worker applies this to itself with sandbox_init(profile, 0, &err) before
; it reads its first request. That calling mode is deprecated and undocumented,
; so the probes in app/src-tauri/tests/probes_macos.rs are the verification.
;
; Deny by default: no network, no file access after startup, no fork or exec,
; no mach lookups (securityd, keychain, pasteboard) and no task ports. The
; worker is already running with fd 0, 1 and 2 open, and reads and writes on
; those descriptors are not mediated by this profile.
;
; Add an allow rule below this line only when a failing probe proves that the
; running worker needs it. Put a comment directly above the
; rule that names the caller and the evidence. No rule is allowed yet: every
; operation the worker performs after init is a read or write on an already
; open descriptor, a memory operation, or a computation. That is an
; expectation, not a result: the profile's first real execution is the CI run
; of the macOS probe jobs.
(deny default)
